version: "2.0"
description: >-
  Gnomon signed platform helper (docs/specs/gnomon.md §3.1, §16, §18). npm
  shell (private) holding the built, signed binaries in bin/ (gitignored build
  output) with checksums.json, verified by the kernel at spawn (G-HLP-01).
  darwin/ is a SwiftPM package (swift-tools 5.9, macOS 14); scripts/ builds
  the signed .app (Developer ID identity looked up in the keychain, the
  provisioning profile embedded from ~/.config/gnomon-signing) and optionally
  notarizes it (keychain profile gnomon-notary). win32/ will be Rust (P8-D71).

components:
  gnomon-helper:
    description: >-
      Holds what the kernel must never hold. M1.3 slice 1: the root and
      approvals P-256 keys in the Secure Enclave (access group
      SW4BMQ8PNL.gnomon, .privateKeyUsage + .userPresence), a sign API over
      stdin/stdout (`serve` NDJSON loop, `once` for one request) speaking
      gnomon-helper:v1 — info, key.create/public/delete, sign (root: fresh
      presence per signature; approvals: fresh, or a per-connection cached
      unlock held here keyed by connId, bounded to 32, dropped after 15 idle
      minutes, 60 minutes after it opened or 64 signatures under it
      (T-2026-10-18-028 M2, helper 1.3.0: hard bounds the idle timer cannot
      slide; the broker enforces the same pair), on unlock.drop and on exit),
      unlock.drop(-all). Each key signs
      only its own domain prefixes (root: row-sig, presence; approvals:
      approve, presence). Inputs bounded before any key is touched. Refuses
      to run sandboxed (P8-D68). Never prints key material. Later: the
      kernel-key keystore item, the keystore log anchor, XPC under launchd,
      the Windows pipe, job objects, WFP, launch-token hand-off.
    path: darwin/Sources/gnomon-helper/
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, helper, native, swift, paradigm-8, secure-enclave, m1.3]
  gnomon-helper-build:
    description: >-
      scripts/build-darwin.mjs (swift build -c release → GnomonHelper.app,
      Info.plist bundle id gnomon.helper, embedded profile, entitlements,
      codesign --options runtime --timestamp with the one Developer ID
      Application identity of team SW4BMQ8PNL found in the keychain, verify
      --strict and against HELPER_REQUIREMENT, sha256 into checksums.json);
      --unsigned for CI. scripts/notarize-darwin.mjs (ditto, notarytool
      submit --keychain-profile gnomon-notary --wait, stapler) is optional and
      founder-run, never run by tests.
    path: scripts/
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, helper, signing, build, m1.3]
